    {
      "id": 496189,
      "username": "sine387",
      "name": "Sine",
      "created_at": "2026-03-22T08:42:05.416Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Jumping straight from 15.33 to 15.69 is usually fine, you don’t need baby steps, but don’t yolo it on prod lol. Just make a full backup, run <code>bench update --patch</code> on staging first, and check custom apps or scripts, that’s where things break 90% of the time. Frappe and ERPNext versions are already close enough, so no weird compatibility issues expected. If staging survives without errors, then push to prod, otherwise you’ll be debugging at 2am wondering why some random doctype exploded.</p>",
